  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\omega=\\frac{z}{z-\\frac{1}{3} i}$ and $|\\omega|=1$, then $z$ lies on",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "O0AAH",
      "text": "\nan ellipse\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tXso9",
      "text": "\na circle\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0cwPO",
      "text": "\na straight line\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ptICZ",
      "text": "\na parabola.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As given $w=\\frac{z}{z-\\frac{1}{3} i} \\Rightarrow|w|=\\frac{|z|}{\\left|z-\\frac{1}{3} i\\right|}=1 \\Rightarrow$ distance of $z$ from origin and point\n$\\left(0, \\frac{1}{3}\\right)$ is same hence $z$ lies on bisector of the line joining points $(0,0)$ and $(0,1 / 3)$.\nHence $z$ lies on a straight line.",
    "image": null
  },
